            <div xml:id="d542">

                <pb facs="0676" n="556" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg556"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00 Revolutions/1: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Puerto Cortes</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wasson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Puerto Cortes</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-04-19T09:00:00-07:00">April 19, 1931—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Armed uprisings took place south and east of San Pedro last night. It is reported
                    that revolutionary forces are accompanied by General Ferrera.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wasson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
